Whether a string has an even number of b's, with a and b the only bytes allowed. The two states, even and odd, are mutually recursive, and each reads the next byte and switches to the other state on a b. Any other byte is a named error.
The probe is mutual recursion over a string, with a named error in the middle of the walk.
---
(lam s
  (mutual ((even (lam l
              (if (? l) 1
                  (let c (head l)
                    (if (= c 97) (even (tail l))
                        (if (= c 98) (odd (tail l)) (raise "bad character")))))))
           (odd (lam l
              (if (? l) 0
                  (let c (head l)
                    (if (= c 97) (odd (tail l))
                        (if (= c 98) (even (tail l)) (raise "bad character"))))))))
    (even s)))
---
"" => 1 fuel 200000
"a" => 1 fuel 200000
"b" => 0 fuel 200000
"abba" => 1 fuel 200000
"bab" => 1 fuel 200000
"aabab" => 1 fuel 200000
"bbb" => 0 fuel 200000
"abc" => error fuel 200000
"a b" => error fuel 200000
